%% param_abstract_covered.glp — POSITIVE guard, case (i) of the abstract-parameter
%% routing matrix (parameterized-types.tex sec:abstract-parameters; spec:
%% docs/type system/typed-program.md "Modular Checking via Abstract Parameters").
%%
%% pdrain/1 is a parameterized procedure that does NOT inspect its parameter (the
%% element position holds the anonymous variable `_`) and does not use its parameter
%% as a type-definition alternative.  It takes the ABSTRACT ROUTE: checked once
%% against its abstract instance pdrain(Stream<$abstract_X>?).
%%
%% Unlike param_free_not_checked.glp, pdrain COVERS the whole Stream input: it has
%% both the [] clause and the [_|Xs] clause.  Its clauses are well-typed by the
%% abstract instance (the element variable is consistent with the abstract type;
%% the tail recurses at the same instance), and every input path is covered.  So by
%% lem:parametricity pdrain is CERTIFIED clean and the file LOADS — even though it
%% is never instantiated.  This is the positive counterpart of case (ii): a clean,
%% fully covered parametric procedure passes the abstract route.
%%
%% Run (from /Users/udi/Grassroots/GLP/glp_runtime/):
%%   printf 'load ../programs/tests/param_abstract_covered.glp\n:quit\n' | bin/glpc

procedure pdrain(Stream(X)?).
pdrain([]).
pdrain([_|Xs]) :- pdrain(Xs?).
